00:57:21.410 --> 00:57:23.140
and you weren't spending
money left and right.

00:57:23.140 --> 00:57:25.570
I know that's not how you were raised.

00:57:25.570 --> 00:57:29.300
But I think for me,

00:57:29.300 --> 00:57:34.220
there was this knowledge of scarcity,

00:57:34.220 --> 00:57:35.730
like, oh my gosh, it's like,

00:57:35.730 --> 00:57:38.500
I mean, we weren't poor
but things were tight.

00:57:38.500 --> 00:57:40.530
And like, I had this
heightened sense of that

00:57:40.530 --> 00:57:43.330
so it was like every single
thing that I would purchase

00:57:43.330 --> 00:57:48.330
or ask for as a kid I just had
this real need to justify it.

00:57:50.200 --> 00:57:52.360
Because I would feel like, you know,

00:57:52.360 --> 00:57:57.360
if I get this Gi Joe Mobile
Command Center for Christmas,

00:57:58.700 --> 00:58:01.380
I mean, how much less
money is that for us like,

00:58:01.380 --> 00:58:02.883
use with something else?

00:58:04.790 --> 00:58:07.190
My mom never talked to me
about any of this stuff

00:58:07.190 --> 00:58:10.060
but it was just something
that I internalized

00:58:10.060 --> 00:58:14.130
and interpreted my situation
as I don't wanna be the reason

00:58:14.130 --> 00:58:15.980
that we go broke.

00:58:15.980 --> 00:58:17.030
And I think that,

00:58:17.030 --> 00:58:19.960
that's kinda stuck with me.

00:58:19.960 --> 00:58:24.450
And it's not fun.

00:58:24.450 --> 00:58:27.050
Well, I think that at this point

00:58:27.050 --> 00:58:28.330
and look what my mom used to tell me.

00:58:28.330 --> 00:58:30.330
But I could buy stuff now
and enjoy it like this.

00:58:30.330 --> 00:58:32.240
My mom used to tell me,

00:58:32.240 --> 00:58:34.700
well I hope you make a lot
of money when you grow up.

00:58:34.700 --> 00:58:37.050
Like that's what she would
say to me all the time.

00:58:37.050 --> 00:58:39.910
Because the way that I
would spend money as a kid,

00:58:39.910 --> 00:58:43.260
like again, my dad had a good job

00:58:43.260 --> 00:58:46.100
and we were well taken care of.

00:58:46.100 --> 00:58:48.210
I mean, still definitely very
much in the middle-class.

00:58:48.210 --> 00:58:53.210
But the interesting thing was

00:58:54.950 --> 00:58:57.770
they didn't buy me a lot of things.

00:58:57.770 --> 00:59:01.210
But what they would do is
they would give me money

00:59:01.210 --> 00:59:02.600
for Christmas or something like that.

00:59:02.600 --> 00:59:05.430
And then what I would do is
I would immediately spend

00:59:05.430 --> 00:59:06.340
all of it, right.

00:59:06.340 --> 00:59:07.173
Yeah.

00:59:07.173 --> 00:59:09.610
I would say, okay, you gave me $50

00:59:09.610 --> 00:59:10.910
for Christmas or whatever.

00:59:12.100 --> 00:59:13.450
All right, let's go to Brendel's.

00:59:13.450 --> 00:59:14.840
I'm gonna spend every bit of it.

00:59:14.840 --> 00:59:16.210
Like why wait?

00:59:16.210 --> 00:59:19.100
Yeah, I had a jar.

00:59:19.100 --> 00:59:23.060
So I wasn't a saver, I've
had to be very disciplined

00:59:23.060 --> 00:59:24.510
about saving as an adult, but

00:59:26.760 --> 00:59:28.860
so that was my disposition already.

00:59:28.860 --> 00:59:30.163
But I do think, and again-

00:59:32.770 --> 00:59:35.280
It can I think simply just
be a personality thing

00:59:35.280 --> 00:59:36.640
because when I look at my three kids,

00:59:36.640 --> 00:59:38.130
like Lincoln, is that way.

00:59:38.130 --> 00:59:41.030
Like he never has money.

00:59:41.030 --> 00:59:43.550
Like the moment he gets money, it's gone.

00:59:43.550 --> 00:59:46.560
And Lando will save up money.

00:59:46.560 --> 00:59:50.110
I had a jar and I would like
meticulously roll up my cash

00:59:50.110 --> 00:59:52.230
and my coins in it.

00:59:52.230 --> 00:59:54.570
And I would say, I can buy this,

00:59:54.570 --> 00:59:58.110
but I don't know something
else will come along.

00:59:58.110 --> 01:00:00.040
I'm just gonna save it till something else

01:00:00.040 --> 01:00:01.577
that like I really gotta get.

01:00:01.577 --> 01:00:05.450
And I would look at the jar and feel good

01:00:05.450 --> 01:00:06.640
you know sense of security.

01:00:06.640 --> 01:00:08.290
Security, yeah.

01:00:08.290 --> 01:00:10.750
Yeah, but Lincoln's
definitely not that way.

01:00:10.750 --> 01:00:15.750
But Lily somewhere in the middle
and Lando is more like me.

01:00:16.340 --> 01:00:17.797
So a lot of is personality based,

01:00:17.797 --> 01:00:18.945
'cause I'm sure the circumstances.

01:00:18.945 --> 01:00:23.650
And I know I mean I'm sure
there's something psychological

01:00:23.650 --> 01:00:27.060
because I do impulse buy things

01:00:27.060 --> 01:00:29.330
and I take comfort in
opening something up.

01:00:29.330 --> 01:00:31.180
Like seeing a box, when
I get home from work,

01:00:31.180 --> 01:00:33.170
seeing a box that was
delivered from Amazon

01:00:33.170 --> 01:00:36.423
and seeing that it's got my name on it.

01:00:36.423 --> 01:00:39.250
'Cause that means is for
me, it's exhilarating.

01:00:39.250 --> 01:00:40.180
And sometimes I'm like,

01:00:40.180 --> 01:00:41.340
I don't even remember what I ordered.

01:00:41.340 --> 01:00:43.590
You know what I'm saying, it's like,

01:00:43.590 --> 01:00:46.850
and so I know that there's
something potentially negative

01:00:46.850 --> 01:00:48.830
about that process as well.

01:00:48.830 --> 01:00:51.060
But I think that the
overarching thing for me

01:00:51.060 --> 01:00:56.060
is neither of us make big purchases.

01:00:57.100 --> 01:00:58.490
Like if we're gonna make a big purchase

01:00:58.490 --> 01:01:00.450
like we're gonna do
this thing on the house.

01:01:00.450 --> 01:01:02.100
And when I say big purchase like,

01:01:02.974 --> 01:01:05.437
I mean we don't buy expensive sports cars,

01:01:05.437 --> 01:01:07.630
we don't buy like boats or something.

01:01:07.630 --> 01:01:09.140
I'm not saying we would never buy a boat

01:01:09.140 --> 01:01:12.570
or something like that if the
opportunity presented itself

01:01:12.570 --> 01:01:15.630
but we don't spend a lot,

01:01:15.630 --> 01:01:17.180
we don't buy big ticket items.

01:01:17.180 --> 01:01:19.950
In fact, sometimes we
don't because we didn't

01:01:19.950 --> 01:01:21.663
like when we started our careers,

01:01:22.650 --> 01:01:25.500
when we were on Santa
Campus Crusade well like,

01:01:25.500 --> 01:01:28.590
we were making very little money,

01:01:28.590 --> 01:01:31.683
like our early marriage both
of us had the same salary.

01:01:33.750 --> 01:01:36.530
I mean, I'll just say what
it was because I remember it,

01:01:36.530 --> 01:01:41.530
we raised $42,000 a year
that was the salary.

01:01:43.500 --> 01:01:46.487
And in North Carolina, 15 years ago,

01:01:46.487 --> 01:01:51.487
$42,000 a year it's not a
lot of money for a family

01:01:52.130 --> 01:01:53.530
with a couple of kids, right.

01:01:53.530 --> 01:01:57.330
Like you have to budget and
you have to kinda think about

01:01:58.450 --> 01:01:59.283
what you're buying.

01:01:59.283 --> 01:02:02.000
And I think that we've
taken that mentality

01:02:02.000 --> 01:02:05.650
as we've made more money,
we've still maintained what,

01:02:05.650 --> 01:02:08.520
again we sometimes we have
to ask our accountant like,

01:02:08.520 --> 01:02:10.890
can you tell us how we're
doing with our money?

01:02:10.890 --> 01:02:13.610
And they're like, you guys
are both very conservative

01:02:13.610 --> 01:02:15.930
because you don't spend a
bunch of money all at once.

01:02:15.930 --> 01:02:17.870
Like yes, there's a bunch
of items that's on this list

01:02:17.870 --> 01:02:20.210
but for me, I feel this freedom

01:02:20.210 --> 01:02:24.880
to spend 10, 20, $30 here and there

01:02:24.880 --> 01:02:29.880
on this kinda steady stream of
pleasurable items for myself

01:02:30.010 --> 01:02:31.530
because I'm not dipping in and going out

01:02:31.530 --> 01:02:34.173
and buying like $100,000 sports
car or something like that.

01:02:34.173 --> 01:02:35.113
I don't do that.

01:02:36.740 --> 01:02:38.660
So I feel like I'm not
being irresponsible,

01:02:38.660 --> 01:02:42.970
